WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:04.480
Dame Ansley!

00:04.480 --> 00:06.330
Please wake up!

00:06.330 --> 00:08.750
What do you mean by "hell"?!

00:09.570 --> 00:11.440
What happened?!

00:15.740 --> 00:18.520
Dame Ansley! Dame Ansley!

00:20.210 --> 00:21.680
<i>Okay, calm down.</i>

00:21.680 --> 00:24.690
<i>It's clear something happened to Noah.</i>

00:25.130 --> 00:27.860
<i>I have to get a search 
party together right away...</i>

00:30.050 --> 00:31.490
Th-The mountain...

00:31.490 --> 00:34.130
The mountain just moved!

00:34.130 --> 00:37.420
What are you talking about? 
Pull yourself together!

00:37.420 --> 00:39.130
The mountain moved?

01:08.740 --> 01:10.490
What is that?

01:25.540 --> 01:26.700
Noah?!

01:31.770 --> 01:33.060
Raeliana.

03:08.500 --> 03:11.590
Maybe it's because the rain 
washed away all the blood,

03:11.590 --> 03:14.500
but I saw no sign of any dragons.

03:14.810 --> 03:19.640
I think, perhaps, there are 
no dragons in the Sycret Mountains.

03:19.640 --> 03:22.140
Dragons? W-Wait just a—

03:22.140 --> 03:25.640
Please accept this instead.

03:26.520 --> 03:27.690
What in the world is that?

03:27.690 --> 03:29.640
I've never seen anything like it.

03:29.640 --> 03:32.640
Th-The duke offered his kill to...

03:33.000 --> 03:34.830
Leave it to the duke.

03:34.830 --> 03:36.800
As for the dragon you wanted...

03:40.080 --> 03:44.660
I promise I'll find one 
in a different mountain range someday.

03:46.760 --> 03:50.370
<i>When did I say I wanted a dragon?!</i>

03:50.370 --> 03:55.680
He never offered a monster 
to anyone before now...

03:58.420 --> 04:01.200
Th-This is... a creoder!

04:01.200 --> 04:02.420
What?!

04:02.420 --> 04:05.250
The one you called the lord 
of the Sycret Mountains?

04:05.250 --> 04:07.880
Remarkable, Your Grace!

04:07.880 --> 04:12.470
It appears Lady McMillan will be the one 
to light the sacred flame this year!

04:16.160 --> 04:18.600
I can't believe you brought down a creoder!

04:18.600 --> 04:21.260
It must have been a grueling effort!

04:21.260 --> 04:24.600
Well, I just happened to come across it.

04:33.510 --> 04:35.740
I thought I'd just grab it quickly...

04:36.080 --> 04:39.840
and use it as bait to catch a dragon.

04:39.840 --> 04:43.440
H-How remarkable...

04:46.130 --> 04:48.180
<i>That poor castle lord...</i>

04:49.530 --> 04:50.750
Raeliana...

04:51.480 --> 04:57.160
I'm terribly sorry it isn't 
the dragon you wanted so badly.

04:57.160 --> 04:58.280
What?

04:58.590 --> 05:01.590
You must have had your 
hopes up quite high.

05:02.780 --> 05:04.940
Miss McMillan wanted a dragon?

05:04.940 --> 05:06.970
Oh, my... a dragon?

05:06.970 --> 05:08.780
A dragon, of all things?

05:08.780 --> 05:11.140
<i>Everyone, you have it all wrong!</i>

05:11.140 --> 05:14.290
<i>I'm not that kind of girl!</i>

05:15.850 --> 05:17.830
Goodness, my Duke.

05:20.340 --> 05:22.830
The rain is soaking you.

05:24.050 --> 05:27.840
You don't smell of alcohol. 
What's this about?

05:28.280 --> 05:31.100
I wish I <i>were</i> drunk, honestly.

05:33.920 --> 05:38.810
For you, I would endure the rain any day.

05:39.810 --> 05:43.810
C-Come inside quickly. You'll catch a cold.

05:43.810 --> 05:45.630
You too, Master Taylor.

06:10.100 --> 06:13.100
Noah! What is the meaning of all this?!

06:13.100 --> 06:16.360
I sent Ansley ahead to inform you.

06:16.870 --> 06:21.280
The effort of trying to catch 
a dragon must have been horrific.

06:21.280 --> 06:24.150
Dame Ansley described it as "hell."

06:24.150 --> 06:27.370
When did I ask for a dragon, exactly?

06:27.370 --> 06:28.410
Adam...

06:30.570 --> 06:32.190
<i>He saw that and thought...</i>

06:33.560 --> 06:36.480
<i>I wish I could toss it 
in the fire right now!</i>

06:36.480 --> 06:38.320
You go change, too.

06:41.870 --> 06:45.370
<i>I'll have to give Adam 
a different handkerchief.</i>

06:45.370 --> 06:47.490
<i>One without a dragon, obviously.</i>

06:47.490 --> 06:49.750
Don't be so disappointed.

06:50.600 --> 06:53.640
I'll find you a dragon 
in another mountain range.

06:54.190 --> 06:57.640
Are you... just teasing me?

06:57.640 --> 06:59.680
You finally caught on?

06:59.690 --> 07:01.120
<i>I want to hit him.</i>

07:01.120 --> 07:04.720
<i>I wish I could hit a pillow 
to calm myself down.</i>

07:04.720 --> 07:05.960
Anyway...

07:05.960 --> 07:06.640
Huh?

07:07.030 --> 07:09.040
How long do you intend to stay?

07:14.040 --> 07:16.160
I'd like to change.

07:17.420 --> 07:21.410
P-Please go ahead! I'll leave now!

07:21.410 --> 07:25.340
If you want to watch, 
you're welcome to stay.

07:26.360 --> 07:27.770
Oh, dear!

07:27.770 --> 07:33.580
For the sake of my eyes, 
please refrain from doing such things!

07:33.580 --> 07:35.800
You're into peeping, right?

07:36.040 --> 07:38.380
<i>Huh? What did he say?</i>

07:38.380 --> 07:42.340
<i>First I'm a clueless rich girl who begs 
for a dragon at a state event,</i>

07:42.340 --> 07:44.350
<i>and now I'm a peeper?!</i>

07:44.350 --> 07:46.840
<i>What kind of character 
is he trying to make me into?</i>

07:46.840 --> 07:50.360
I do wish you wouldn't keep 
saying such nonsensical things.

07:50.360 --> 07:51.670
Nonsensical?

07:51.670 --> 07:54.380
Then when you were secretly 
watching me sleep that ti—

07:57.950 --> 08:01.610
That wasn't because I'm 
"into" anything like that...

08:01.610 --> 08:03.680
Anyway, you're mistaken!

08:03.680 --> 08:06.460
I apologized for that, didn't I?

08:06.460 --> 08:11.210
Also, you were watching me 
when I was sleeping in bed, too!

08:12.000 --> 08:13.280
That time?

08:13.920 --> 08:15.280
Oh...

08:15.280 --> 08:18.220
When you thought 
I'd assaulted you in your sleep,

08:18.490 --> 08:22.190
and you cried out like 
the world was coming to an end?

08:22.680 --> 08:24.680
When did I "cry out"?

08:24.680 --> 08:28.560
You're the one who gave me 
the wrong idea in the first place!

08:29.820 --> 08:31.010
I'm sorry.

08:31.480 --> 08:34.000
You even apologized for it, didn't you?!

08:34.360 --> 08:36.330
<i>This jerk!</i>

08:39.780 --> 08:43.750
Noah, didn't you know?

08:46.240 --> 08:50.750
Nobody likes men who fixate 
on other people's mistakes.

08:54.100 --> 08:55.880
Understand?

09:01.060 --> 09:02.800
<i>He's acting awfully meek.</i>

09:02.800 --> 09:06.900
Promise me you'll never 
bring this up again!

09:06.900 --> 09:08.440
All right?

09:08.440 --> 09:09.670
Well, then...

09:09.670 --> 09:12.900
I'm sure you're exhausted. 
Please get some rest.

09:28.920 --> 09:32.800
<i>How could I have done 
something like that to a duke?</i>

09:32.800 --> 09:38.920
<i>I feel like... I've come 
a bit closer to him.</i>

09:39.600 --> 09:41.700
Are you returning to your room?

09:42.720 --> 09:44.420
Allow me to escort you.

09:47.640 --> 09:52.220
The lady knight you arrived 
with has made quite the recovery.

09:52.220 --> 09:54.710
She's resting in a separate room.

09:55.080 --> 09:57.950
Thank you... and, um...

09:58.130 --> 10:00.730
Is the castle lord all right?

10:00.730 --> 10:02.040
Yes...

10:02.040 --> 10:06.920
He keeps shouting "Creoder!" 
as he drowns his frustrations in drink.

10:06.920 --> 10:08.300
Ah...

10:08.300 --> 10:09.640
Forgive me, but...

10:09.640 --> 10:10.520
Yes?

10:10.960 --> 10:15.970
Is it true that His Grace 
was insistent on finding a dragon?

10:15.970 --> 10:19.350
Actually, that was sort of 
a misunderstanding...

10:38.860 --> 10:42.880
I was worried when you were late returning,

10:42.880 --> 10:44.800
but I'm glad you're safe.

10:45.740 --> 10:47.760
As if you really mean that.

10:48.650 --> 10:52.500
It's a relief to see you 
haven't changed a bit.

10:54.600 --> 10:55.970
What does that mean?

10:56.620 --> 10:59.580
I feel bad for that creoder, 
the lord of the mountains,

10:59.580 --> 11:03.610
if you really killed it just for sport.

11:03.610 --> 11:05.290
For sport?

11:05.290 --> 11:06.390
Yes.

11:06.830 --> 11:11.180
Am I wrong? If so, 
I find it a bit concerning.

11:12.400 --> 11:16.630
That was your first time catching 
a monster during the hunt, yes?

11:16.900 --> 11:20.980
It was my first time bringing one back.

11:21.960 --> 11:23.910
Right. And...

11:24.400 --> 11:28.910
It was your first time 
offering one to a lady, as well.

11:29.830 --> 11:31.360
What's your point?

11:32.160 --> 11:35.060
Oh, just that it doesn't seem like you.

11:36.100 --> 11:40.280
That aside, what of
 the matter with Duke Blake?

11:41.570 --> 11:46.910
There are rumors that he has grown quite 
close to a certain woman of late.

11:46.910 --> 11:47.940
A woman?

11:47.940 --> 11:52.190
Whitton is currently looking 
into her identity.

11:52.690 --> 11:54.330
A woman, eh?

11:55.230 --> 11:58.680
I hope he doesn't ruin himself 
over something stupid.

11:59.960 --> 12:02.800
Some say women are monsters,

12:02.800 --> 12:07.460
but, at times, they can 
be far more terrifying.

12:07.460 --> 12:10.550
If there's something you 
want to say, just say it.

12:12.460 --> 12:16.660
Noah, I'm asking you this 
as your aide and friend.

12:17.250 --> 12:18.470
Let's hear it.

12:19.210 --> 12:21.960
Are you serious about Miss McMillan?

12:22.450 --> 12:23.560
No.

12:24.920 --> 12:27.220
That's what you wanted to ask?

12:27.220 --> 12:29.480
You've been acting strange lately.

12:29.480 --> 12:32.290
I think you're the one who's acting strange.

12:35.240 --> 12:39.480
Then if I were to pursue Miss McMillan,

12:39.480 --> 12:41.290
you'd be fine with that?

12:43.810 --> 12:45.600
What are you saying,

12:46.240 --> 12:48.950
Keith Westernberg?

12:52.320 --> 12:54.200
Remember your place.

12:59.590 --> 13:00.630
Right.

13:24.190 --> 13:26.420
<i>It's all mine.</i>

13:27.560 --> 13:32.030
<i>Every single man I meet 
showers me with adoration.</i>

13:32.030 --> 13:35.030
<i>A bisque doll with 
glittering eyes of gold...</i>

13:35.680 --> 13:39.550
<i>A beautiful woman who bears 
the scent of a pink rose...</i>

13:40.490 --> 13:45.220
<i>The teeth behind these red lips 
shine like diamonds, they say.</i>

13:45.730 --> 13:48.670
<i>These long legs that look 
so lovely in lace stockings</i>

13:48.670 --> 13:50.850
<i>captivate all men, they say.</i>

13:52.350 --> 13:55.750
<i>No matter how hated I was 
or what anyone said,</i>

13:55.750 --> 13:58.170
<i>I was always the winner.</i>

13:58.710 --> 14:03.120
<i>I had everything, and getting 
what I wanted was easy...</i>

14:04.430 --> 14:06.630
<i>Until I met that man.</i>

14:17.990 --> 14:22.090
<i>The only reason I accepted 
the proposal of that limping king</i>

14:22.090 --> 14:25.600
<i>was to make him regret turning me down.</i>

14:26.560 --> 14:29.360
<i>I was supposed to light the temple's 
sacred flame again this year,</i>

14:29.360 --> 14:33.590
<i>while looking down on him and his fiancée.</i>

14:36.780 --> 14:38.080
<i>And yet...</i>

14:45.490 --> 14:48.790
<i>I can't bear the thought of 
him not becoming mine!</i>

15:09.150 --> 15:11.570
There's something you want, right?

15:13.800 --> 15:16.090
This will help you.

15:31.100 --> 15:33.800
What? Vivian Shamal's leaving?

15:33.800 --> 15:37.670
Yes. She is returning to her mansion.

15:37.670 --> 15:40.640
So she won't be going to the temple?

15:40.640 --> 15:42.290
Correct.

15:42.290 --> 15:46.880
But doesn't everyone go to the temple 
after the hunt every year?

15:46.880 --> 15:47.830
Yes,

15:47.830 --> 15:52.670
but none of the ladies 
are obligated to go except for you,

15:52.670 --> 15:56.310
as the one who will light the sacred flame.

15:56.870 --> 15:58.850
I see.

15:58.850 --> 16:02.190
We will depart for the temple 
as soon as you are ready.

16:02.190 --> 16:03.530
Please continue.

16:03.540 --> 16:04.930
All right.

16:07.210 --> 16:11.460
<i>I mean, not only is she not 
lighting the sacred flame,</i>

16:11.460 --> 16:13.480
<i>but I'm the one doing it.</i>

16:13.480 --> 16:16.570
<i>I guess I can't blame her 
for not wanting to go.</i>

16:17.030 --> 16:19.370
<i>Maybe I went a little too far...</i>

16:24.640 --> 16:26.680
Your Holiness Heika,

16:26.680 --> 16:30.090
you really don't intend to go?

16:30.090 --> 16:32.900
Why should I go out of my way to be there

16:32.900 --> 16:36.090
just for the sake 
of a bunch of petty nobles?

16:36.430 --> 16:40.280
But Duke Wynknight will be 
in attendance this time.

16:40.280 --> 16:42.570
That is what I've come to tell you.

16:44.170 --> 16:45.750
<i>He's not even listening...</i>

16:46.360 --> 16:51.700
<i>He has always detested nobles, 
regarding them as selfish fools.</i>

16:52.610 --> 16:57.710
<i>But this is the one time 
I can't afford to back down!</i>

16:57.710 --> 17:02.080
Our organization's financial 
situation is worsening.

17:04.620 --> 17:07.550
Donations have decreased 
with each passing year,

17:07.550 --> 17:11.590
and our organization's internal 
operations are struggling.

17:11.960 --> 17:17.910
The monster hunt is our best opportunity 
to get donations from the nobles!

17:18.410 --> 17:20.590
And above all, residing in the temple right now

17:20.600 --> 17:26.390
is the great priest and legend 
who changed theology as we knew it:

17:26.390 --> 17:30.490
the great Heika Demint himself!

17:33.400 --> 17:36.490
This is clearly divine guidance!

17:36.490 --> 17:42.040
So I'm required to personally attend 
every little thing, you dumb shit?

17:42.040 --> 17:43.430
Sh-Shi—

17:45.230 --> 17:47.270
<i>I can't lose heart now!</i>

17:47.630 --> 17:50.310
Letting the current conditions 
continue would hinder

17:50.310 --> 17:53.550
our theological research 
and the upbringing of the next generation!

17:53.550 --> 17:54.920
What?

17:54.920 --> 17:56.740
You are surprisingly—

17:56.740 --> 17:58.190
I mean,

17:58.190 --> 18:00.680
you have always wanted nothing more than

18:00.680 --> 18:02.930
the best education 
for your pupils, have you not?

18:02.930 --> 18:06.000
Well, maybe if <i>you</i> were a smarter disciple

18:06.000 --> 18:08.750
who could advance my research along with me,

18:08.750 --> 18:12.570
it would've shaved five 
years off our studies!

18:12.780 --> 18:18.570
Then we could've saved five years' worth of 
funds rather than spending it frivolously!

18:18.570 --> 18:21.950
Are you telling me that's 
not your own stupid fault?!

18:21.950 --> 18:24.310
I, Wade Davis,

18:24.310 --> 18:25.440
despite appearances,

18:25.440 --> 18:29.100
graduated top of my class from 
the Fyatt International School of Theology!

18:29.100 --> 18:31.400
I may not be the genius you are,

18:31.400 --> 18:34.640
but I can confidently say 
I qualify as a prodigy!

18:34.640 --> 18:38.220
The school of theology will take 
just any idiot these days, huh?

18:38.220 --> 18:39.970
Your Holiness!

18:40.400 --> 18:42.770
Judging by your character,

18:42.770 --> 18:47.980
I bet that squawking parrot mouth of yours 
is gonna be why you die young!

18:47.980 --> 18:51.910
What are you saying?! 
You can't see my character at all!

18:51.910 --> 18:53.640
Yeah, that's right!

18:53.640 --> 18:58.030
No one can see your character under 
that clay mask you call a face!

18:58.030 --> 19:01.080
That has nothing to do with character! 
That'd just be a curse!

19:01.080 --> 19:02.510
Shut up!

19:02.510 --> 19:07.090
I'm just advising you to keep quiet, 
work hard, and live a happy life!

19:07.090 --> 19:09.290
So shut your trap and listen!

19:13.350 --> 19:18.190
<i>Oh, God, please grant me the strength 
to claim victory against this geezer.</i>

19:18.810 --> 19:21.620
Your Holiness, please listen to me.

19:22.130 --> 19:24.820
As far as those petty nobles are concerned,

19:25.190 --> 19:29.510
even the briefest appearance by you, 
the head of our organization,

19:29.510 --> 19:32.320
carries unspeakably tremendous value.

19:32.830 --> 19:36.710
A mere word of greeting 
and a handshake from you

19:36.710 --> 19:41.310
would bring in enough donations to keep 
the temple running for another year.

19:41.320 --> 19:46.810
Your Holiness, all it takes is 
for you to simply show your face.

19:47.400 --> 19:50.770
<i>He's always been a very proud man.</i>

19:50.770 --> 19:53.440
<i>He can't ignore my request 
after hearing all that!</i>

19:53.440 --> 19:56.840
Well... I suppose so. Wade,

19:56.840 --> 19:58.070
come here.

19:58.070 --> 19:59.840
You finally understand?!

20:00.990 --> 20:02.520
Get out of here.

20:09.350 --> 20:14.350
Raeliana, I'll be heading 
to the temple first.

20:14.350 --> 20:16.580
Have a safe trip.

20:18.830 --> 20:23.070
I look forward to the ceremonial 
lighting of the sacred flame.

20:24.380 --> 20:28.070
What a man!

20:33.120 --> 20:36.460
Miss McMillan, greetings to you.

20:37.640 --> 20:41.560
I will pray for the success 
of the ceremonial lighting.

20:41.920 --> 20:44.230
Th-Thank you.

21:04.400 --> 21:07.510
<i>Was that in my luggage?</i>

21:08.780 --> 21:10.520
Lady McMillan.

21:10.910 --> 21:13.630
Whitton was at the mansion running errands,

21:13.630 --> 21:15.650
and Gideon left this with him.

21:16.510 --> 21:17.700
Thank you.

21:17.700 --> 21:20.020
It's time for us to depart.

21:20.020 --> 21:21.410
Okay.

21:25.570 --> 21:27.930
It's all mine.

22:42.470 --> 22:44.780
The Fyatt International 
School of Theology...

22:45.910 --> 22:49.810
"I am writing in response 
to the matter you asked about.

22:50.370 --> 22:54.450
A student by the name of Beatrice Trancet...

22:56.020 --> 22:57.940
does not attend this school."

22:59.560 --> 23:03.060
<i>Beatrice isn't there? 
Did she come back home?</i>

23:05.080 --> 23:07.960
<i>Or is she somewhere completely different?</i>

23:08.870 --> 23:15.900
<i>Originally, she came back because I, 
Raeliana McMillan, died...</i>

23:17.380 --> 23:19.240
<i>But I survived.</i>

23:20.130 --> 23:22.290
<i>So because of me...</i>

23:23.480 --> 23:26.680
The things that happen 
from now on might change?

23:30.000 --> 23:31.580
<i>Beatrice...</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:39.980
<b>Episode Nine</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:39.980
<b>Why Raeliana Was Called a Barbarian</b>
